st  want them all to know that they're in  our hearts today but you know you you  just recited a lot of progress on  reopening America and I must tell you  the President and I are very confident  that as as now all 50 states have begun  the process of reopening our country  that while there may be instances where  where people are or would would do well  to be reminded about the importance of  social distancing and the importance of  continuing regular hygiene we have every  confidence that that as as these  restrictions are more loosened in the  days ahead the American people are going  to step forward and put this country  back to work in a safe and in  responsible way mr. vice president the  president tweeted about schools he said  schools in our country should be opened  ASAP much very good information now  available what's the latest on this  because we're many people in New York  City for instance are wondering should  are their kids gonna be going back to  school if not should we enroll them  somewhere else well you know it's  important to reflect today on two things  I think Ainsley number one is the the  more than 98 thousand Americans who've  lost their lives our hearts are with  their families on this Memorial Day as  well but but I think we also do well to  reflect on the fact that because the  American people embrace the president's  leadership listen to state and local  authorities that tens of thousands of  families have been spared the heartache  of that loss and we've seen real  progress all across the country  I mean hospitalizations are declining  we've seen a steady decline in cases and  new cases across the country and most  importantly fatalities continue to  decline you saw the governor of New York  as you mentioned their state say that  New York is essentially back where they  started back in March and so we are we  are on the far side  of this epidemic in in many of the  places most impacted and that's given us  an opportunity not just the issue as we  did now more than a month ago the  guidelines to open up America again but  the CDC and the task force are going to  continue to produce useful information  about about how we can bring back our  schools how we can bring back summer  camps how we can go back to churches and  synagogues and mosques and enjoy in a  safe and responsible way our freedoms of  religion so what we're working very  closely with university presidents  around the country over the last several  weeks we'll be welcoming them to the  White House soon and we have every  confidence that whether it be our  universities around the country or  whether it be a primary and secondary  education that we're in in most areas of  the country we're going to be able to  get kids back to school in a safe and  responsible way mr. vice president thank  you very much for joining us this  morning you know there is an ongoing  tension between blue state governor's  governor's that are keeping states  locked down a little bit more in the  uncertainty that that creates I've got  to ask you because the president just  put out a tweet just moments ago and it  pertains to this and we want to get your  reaction he tweeted this he said I love  the great state of North Carolina so  much so that I insisted on having the  RNC the Republican National Convention  in Charlotte at the end of August  unfortunately Democrat governor Roy  Cooper is still in shutdown mood and  unable to guarantee that by August we  will be allowed full attendance in the  arena in other words we would be  spending millions of dollars building  the arena to a very high standard  without even knowing if the Democrat  governor would allow the Republican  Party to fully occupy the space plans  are being made by many thousands of  enthusiastic Republicans and others to  head to North Carolina in August they  must be immediately given an answer by  the governor as to whether or not the  space will be allowed to be fully  occupied if not we will be reluctantly  forced to find with all the jobs and  economic development it brings another  Republican National Convention site this  is not something I want to do thank you  and I love the people of North Carolina  so this is a a macro look at something  that's happened at the smaller level as  well governor's locking down decisions  can't be made businesses being  hit first if you would to the RNC in the  convention and the possibility of  changing it and then that question  overall well it's an issue we've been  talking about Pete because these  national conventions literally take many  months to organize and prepare and and  you know there are states around the  country we think of Texas we think of  Florida Georgia the last two states I  visited last week that have made a  tremendous progress on reopening their  communities and reopening their  economies and I think the president is  is absolutely intent on ensuring that as  we see our nation continue to make  steady progress on putting the corona  virus epidemic in the past that come  this August will be able to come  together in a in a safe and responsible  venue and INRI nominate president Donald  Trump for four more years but what what  you hear the president saying today is  just a very reasonable request of the  governor of North Carolina we all want  to be in Charlotte we love North  Carolina but having a sense now is  absolutely essential because of the  immense preparations that are involved  and we look forward to working with the  governor Cooper getting a swift response  and and if needs be if needs be moving  the national convention to a state that  that is farther along on reopening and  and can say with confidence that that we  can gather there mr. vice president  earlier in today's program we talked to  a couple of guys who owned a diner in  Pennsylvania York Pennsylvania and they  reopened on Mother's Day weekend despite  the the fact that the governor kept the  state closed down they defied the order  they appeared on our program I think  about four days ago and within just a  few hours then the state suspended their  license and said you got to close they  are still open this morning we talked to  them listen to what they had to say  earlier  governor wolf through a little  tyrannical temper tantrum  and decided to just you know suspend our  is it through emergency powers to  suspend our licenses but it's not about  a diner it's about the American people  they want the freedom every customer  comes in they thank us thank you being  open  we provide something that the community  needs right now to flatten this fear and  progress forward flatten the fear mr.  vice president can you understand the  frustration with certain business owners  in certain locations that have not  reopened yet well I really can't Steven  it's it's the reason why even before the  the 45 days to slow the spread president  Trump had us issue guidelines to open up  America again and and we made it clear  to Governor wolf and governors across  the country that they could implement  that guidance not just on a statewide  basis but on a county-by-county basis  and this last week I actually was able  to to grab lunch in a nice diner in in  Georgia another one in Florida I think  the American people see that we we can  safely and responsibly reopen our  restaurants in many places around the  country and we're just going to continue  to urge governor wolf and other  governors around the country to look for  those opportunities not to use the  coercive power of the state but to find  ways to to literally restore the  freedoms that we all cherish this is a  freedom-loving country today we feel on  our hearts a particular weight of  gratitude to the people who fought and  died for that freedom and we're just  going to continue in all of our  interactions with governor's around the  country to encourage them to restore  their economies reopen their country and  we're working in full partnership with  governor's to make sure they have the  testing supplies and resources and PPE  necessary to be able to accomplish that  in a way that puts the health of their  citizens even right alongside the health  of a growing economy  mr. vice president we heard the airplane  flying it reminds me the airforce and  all of the branches that I know your son  is serving Pete you have served my dad  served my grandfather's Steve I know  Minnie and your family have served what  is your message on this Memorial Day by  the way I read your op-ed on foxnews.com  it's called this Memorial Day our  freedoms are cherished even more and  here is why it was beautifully written  but what's your message for our great  country thank you  well this message on this Memorial Day  even in the midst of these challenging  times is that this freedom loving nation  knows that freedom isn't free and we are  grateful every day for all of the men  and women who serve in the Army Navy Air  Force Marines and Coast Guard but  today's the day that we remember those  who served and fell in battle and when  the President and I and the first lady  and Karen gathered in just a few moments  at Arlington will lay a wreath will say  a prayer and I just encourage people  across this country to remember the  families of our fallen in your prayers  especially this day when you see people  out waving flags and standing up for  freedom across the country during these  challenging times this Memorial Day I  think we do feel a special special  weight of gratitude to those who  defended that freedom throughout our  history who paid the ultimate sacrifice  for our freedom and they are in our  hearts today they're in our prayers and  to each of them I want them to know this  Memorial Day we are grateful to them and  and their loved ones who who  demonstrated that what the Bible says is  no greater love the Lord says that no  greater love as a man than this then he  should lay down his life for his friends  and today we remember all the men and  women throughout our history who have  laid down their lives for our freedom  indeed mr. vice president thank you very  much we will see you in the president at  the tomb of the you know unknowns very  shortly at Arlington thank you very much  thank you so much

